IMPORT prelude

-- Precious Stones and Precious Metals (Prevention of Money Laundering, Terrorism Financing and Proliferation Financing) Act 2019
-- (Singapore) -- who is a regulated dealer (s 2 and the Schedule), the duty to register (s 6), refusal, lapse and regulatory action
-- (ss 8, 9A, 10, 11, 13), the $20,000 cash threshold and the duties it triggers (ss 15, 16, 17), and the maximum penalties
-- (ss 6, 16-22, 27, 28) with composition (s 31).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021), informal consolidation (version in force from
-- 1/5/2024), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PSPMPMLTFPFA2019.txt; the latest amendment annotated is Act 6 of 2024
-- wef 01/05/2024 (54 annotations), with one by Act 18 of 2022 wef 28/04/2023. Retrieved 1 October 2026 as the current version.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0073 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to what a jeweller, gold dealer or watch seller meets. Not encoded: appointments (ss 4, 5), conditions of
-- registration (s 9), recovery of penalties (s 12), the content of the due-diligence, record-keeping, programme and sanctions duties
-- (ss 18-20, all "prescribed" -- the regulations were not retrieved), directions (s 22) beyond their penalty, the monitoring,
-- investigation and seizure powers (ss 23-26), foreign disclosure, immunity, corporate liability and procedure (ss 29-40).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Precious Stones and Precious Metals Act 2019 -- dealers`

§§ `The Schedule -- precious metals and precious stones`

-- Part 1, precious metals: "1. Gold 2. Silver 3. Platinum 4. Iridium 5. Osmium 6. Palladium 7. Rhodium 8. Ruthenium 9. An alloy with at
-- least 2% in weight of any substance mentioned in items 1 to 8". s 2: a precious metal is one in Part 1 "in a manufactured or
-- unmanufactured state".
-- Part 2, "PRECIOUS STONES (NATURAL OR OTHERWISE)": "1. Diamond 2. Sapphire 3. Ruby 4. Emerald 5. Jade (including nephrite and
-- jadeite) 6. Pearl". (Inference: "natural or otherwise" takes in laboratory-grown stones.)
DECLARE Material IS ONE OF
    gold
    silver
    platinum
    iridium
    osmium
    palladium
    rhodium
    ruthenium
    diamond
    `a laboratory-grown diamond`
    sapphire
    ruby
    emerald
    jade
    pearl
    copper
    titanium
    opal
    amethyst

GIVEN `the material` IS A Material
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is a precious metal` IF
    CONSIDER `the material`
    WHEN gold THEN TRUE
    WHEN silver THEN TRUE
    WHEN platinum THEN TRUE
    WHEN iridium THEN TRUE
    WHEN osmium THEN TRUE
    WHEN palladium THEN TRUE
    WHEN rhodium THEN TRUE
    WHEN ruthenium THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the material` IS A Material
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is a precious stone` IF
    CONSIDER `the material`
    WHEN diamond THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a laboratory-grown diamond` THEN TRUE
    WHEN sapphire THEN TRUE
    WHEN ruby THEN TRUE
    WHEN emerald THEN TRUE
    WHEN jade THEN TRUE
    WHEN pearl THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- Part 1 item 9: "at least 2% in weight" -- exactly 2% counts.
GIVEN `percent by weight of items 1 to 8` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the alloy is a precious metal` IF
    `percent by weight of items 1 to 8` AT LEAST 2

§§ `2 -- precious product`

-- "precious product" means any jewellery, watch, apparel, accessory, ornament or other finished product -- (a) made up of, containing
-- or having attached to it, any precious stone or precious metal or both; and (b) that satisfies either of the following: (i) "at
-- least 50% of the value ... (or other percentage of value prescribed in substitution) is attributable to the precious stone or
-- precious metal or both"; (ii) it "is priced above the prescribed value", "but excludes any product or class of products of a type
-- prescribed". The prescribed value is not in the Act; it is a parameter here.
GIVEN `contains a precious stone or metal` IS A BOOLEAN, `percent of value from the stone or metal` IS A NUMBER,
      `the price` IS A NUMBER, `the prescribed value` IS A NUMBER, `of a prescribed excluded type` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the finished product is a precious product` IF
        `contains a precious stone or metal`
    AND (    `percent of value from the stone or metal` AT LEAST 50
         OR  `the price` GREATER THAN `the prescribed value`)
    AND (NOT `of a prescribed excluded type`)

§§ `2 -- regulated dealer`

-- "regulated dealing" means doing any of the following: (a) manufacturing any precious stone, precious metal or precious product; (b)
-- importing or possessing for sale any ...; (c) selling or offering for sale any ...; (d) "selling or redeeming asset-backed tokens";
-- (e) "purchasing any precious stone, precious metal or precious product for the purposes of resale".
-- "regulated dealer" means any person who carries on -- (a) a business of regulated dealing; or (b) business as an intermediary for
-- regulated dealing, "but excludes a pawnbroker and any other person as may be prescribed".
-- (The deposit prints the "intermediary" definition followed by "[Deleted by Act 6 of 2024 wef 01/05/2024]". Limb (b) still uses the
-- word, so this encoding keeps it; which definition the annotation refers to is not clear from the deposit.)
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    manufacturing
    `importing or possessing for sale`
    `selling or offering for sale`
    `selling or redeeming asset-backed tokens`
    `purchasing for resale`
    `acting as an intermediary for regulated dealing`
    `buying for personal use`
    `repairing for a fee`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is regulated dealing` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `buying for personal use` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `repairing for a fee` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity, `carried on as a business` IS A BOOLEAN, `the goods are in scope` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a pawnbroker` IS A BOOLEAN, `is otherwise prescribed out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a regulated dealer` IF
        `the activity is regulated dealing` `the activity`
    AND `carried on as a business`
    AND `the goods are in scope`
    AND (NOT `is a pawnbroker`)
    AND (NOT `is otherwise prescribed out`)

§§ `6 -- no regulated dealing without registration`

-- s 6(1): "A person must not act as or hold out to be a regulated dealer unless the person is a registered dealer." (2): a fine not
-- exceeding $75,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 3 years or both, "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- exceeding $7,500 for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `acts as a regulated dealer` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds out to be a regulated dealer` IS A BOOLEAN, `is registered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unregistered dealing is an offence` IF
    (`acts as a regulated dealer` OR `holds out to be a regulated dealer`) AND (NOT `is registered`)

GIVEN `days or part days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unregistered dealing` MEANS
    75000 PLUS 7500 TIMES `days or part days continued after conviction`

§§ `8 -- grounds for refusing registration`

-- s 8(1): the Registrar MAY refuse on any of: (a) fee not paid; (b) the application contains materially false or misleading
-- information, or is materially incomplete; (c) the applicant is not a fit and proper person; (d) a substantial shareholder,
-- director, manager, partner, secretary, compliance officer or managing employee is not; (e) not in the public interest.
GIVEN `fee unpaid` IS A BOOLEAN, `materially false or incomplete` IS A BOOLEAN, `applicant not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a key person not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN, `against the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse registration` IF
        `fee unpaid`
    OR  `materially false or incomplete`
    OR  `applicant not fit and proper`
    OR  `a key person not fit and proper`
    OR  `against the public interest`

-- s 8(2)(a): the Registrar must have regard to whether the person has been convicted, "whether in Singapore or elsewhere", (i) "of an
-- offence involving fraud or dishonesty punishable with imprisonment for a term of 3 months or more", or (ii) "of a relevant offence"
-- (Parts 2, 3, 5; CDSA ss 50-57; terrorism financing; UN Act regulations; foreign AML/CFT/CPF law). The weight is the Registrar's.
GIVEN `involves fraud or dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER, `is a relevant offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction is a fitness matter` IF
        (`involves fraud or dishonesty` AND `maximum imprisonment in months` AT LEAST 3)
    OR  `is a relevant offence`

§§ `9A -- lapse`

-- s 9A: registration lapses "(a) when the registered dealer (being an entity) is wound up or otherwise dissolved, whether in Singapore
-- or elsewhere; or (b) when the registered dealer (being an individual who is a sole proprietor) dies."
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `the company is wound up`
    `the entity is dissolved abroad`
    `the sole proprietor dies`
    `a director dies`
    `the company changes its name`

GIVEN `the event` IS A Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registration lapses` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `the company is wound up` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the entity is dissolved abroad` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the sole proprietor dies` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `10, 11 -- regulatory action`

-- s 10(1): the Registrar may cancel, "or suspend the registration for a period not exceeding 6 months". (2): "in addition to or
-- instead of" that, a financial penalty "not exceeding $100,000", where the dealer "(a) contravenes a provision of this Act, which
-- contravention is not an offence; or (b) fails to comply with a condition of registration".
GIVEN `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension is within the limit` IF
    `months` AT MOST 6

GIVEN `contravention that is not an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `breach of a registration condition` IS A BOOLEAN, `the penalty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the financial penalty may be ordered` IF
        (`contravention that is not an offence` OR `breach of a registration condition`)
    AND `the penalty` AT MOST 100000

-- s 11(1)(c): the notice must give a time for representations "being at least 14 days after the date the written notice is served",
-- unless notice "is not practicable or desirable".
GIVEN `days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `notice not practicable or desirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice period is sufficient` IF
    `notice not practicable or desirable` OR `days allowed` AT LEAST 14

§§ `13 -- appeal to the Minister`

-- s 13(1): appeal lies against (a) refusal to grant or renew; (b) imposing or adding, varying or cancelling a condition; (c) any
-- regulatory action under s 10. (2) the appeal "does not affect the validity of the decision" and it "must be complied with until the
-- determination of the appeal" (and s 11(4)). (4) the decision on appeal "is final".
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusal to register`
    `refusal to renew`
    `a new condition`
    `cancellation`
    `suspension`
    `a financial penalty`
    `a written direction under section 22`
    `lapse on winding up`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is appealable to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a written direction under section 22` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `lapse on winding up` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `15 -- designated transaction and the threshold amount`

-- s 15 "designated transaction" (conducted wholly or partly in Singapore): (a) a sale by a regulated dealer to a customer "for which
-- cash or a cash equivalent exceeding the threshold amount is received"; (b) "2 or more sales ... in a single day ... to the same
-- customer", or to customers known to act for the same person, "for which cash or a cash equivalent in total exceeding the threshold
-- amount is received"; (c) a purchase from a customer "(who is not a regulated dealer) by a regulated dealer (who is a secondhand goods
-- dealer)" paid in cash exceeding the threshold; (d) prescribed. "threshold amount" means "$20,000 or its equivalent in value".
-- "cash" means "currency notes and coins"; "cash equivalent" is whatever is prescribed. (Inference: card and bank payments are not cash.)
DECLARE Kind IS ONE OF
    `a sale to a customer`
    `a purchase from a customer`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`the threshold amount` MEANS 20000

GIVEN `the kind` IS A Kind, `cash in this transaction` IS A NUMBER, `cash from the same customer in sales that day` IS A NUMBER,
      `the dealer is a secondhand goods dealer` IS A BOOLEAN, `the customer is a regulated dealer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transaction is designated` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a sale to a customer` THEN
            `cash in this transaction` GREATER THAN `the threshold amount`
        OR  `cash from the same customer in sales that day` GREATER THAN `the threshold amount`
    WHEN `a purchase from a customer` THEN
            `cash in this transaction` GREATER THAN `the threshold amount`
        AND `the dealer is a secondhand goods dealer`
        AND (NOT `the customer is a regulated dealer`)

§§ `16, 17 -- customer due diligence and cash transaction reports`

-- s 16(1): the dealer must perform the prescribed CDD measures "(a) before entering into a designated transaction; (b) where the
-- regulated dealer has reason to suspect money laundering, terrorism financing or the financing of proliferation ...; (c) where the
-- regulated dealer has reason to doubt the veracity or adequacy of information obtained from earlier customer due diligence".
-- (4): unless (3) applies, the dealer "may choose not to perform or to complete" a measure if it suspects the transaction relates to
-- ML/TF/PF AND believes performing it "will tip off the customer".
GIVEN `designated` IS A BOOLEAN, `reason to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN, `doubts earlier CDD` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `customer due diligence is required` IF
    `designated` OR `reason to suspect` OR `doubts earlier CDD`

GIVEN `reason to suspect` IS A BOOLEAN, `believes CDD would tip off` IS A BOOLEAN, `a prescribed bar under 16(3) exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealer may skip due diligence to avoid tipping off` IF
    `reason to suspect` AND `believes CDD would tip off` AND (NOT `a prescribed bar under 16(3) exists`)

-- s 16(5): where the dealer "is for any reason unable or chooses not to complete" a measure, it must "(a) decline to enter into any
-- transaction with the customer; (b) terminate any transaction entered into", (c) determine whether to file a suspicious transaction
-- disclosure and (d) record the basis.
GIVEN `CDD required` IS A BOOLEAN, `CDD completed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealer must decline or terminate` IF
    `CDD required` AND (NOT `CDD completed`)

-- s 17(1): a dealer "who enters into any designated transaction must submit to a Suspicious Transaction Reporting Officer, within the
-- prescribed time, a cash transaction report"; (3) and a copy to the Registrar "at the time ... or immediately thereafter".
GIVEN `entered into a designated transaction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a cash transaction report is due` IF
    `entered into a designated transaction`

§§ `6, 16-22, 27, 28, 31 -- maximum penalties and composition`

-- s 6(2) $75,000 / 3 years; s 16(6) CDD $100,000; s 17(4) cash transaction reports $20,000 / 2 years; s 18(5) records $100,000;
-- s 19(3) programmes $100,000; s 20(2) targeted financial sanctions $100,000; s 21(3) failing to copy a disclosure to the Registrar
-- $20,000; s 22(5) failing to comply with a written direction $20,000; s 27 false information $50,000 / 2 years; s 28 obstruction
-- $50,000 / 2 years. Sections 16, 18, 19, 20, 21 and 22 carry a fine only.
-- s 31(1): the Registrar may compound a prescribed compoundable offence for "a sum not exceeding half of the amount of the maximum fine".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unregistered dealing`
    `failing to do customer due diligence`
    `failing to file a cash transaction report`
    `failing to keep records`
    `no adequate AML programme`
    `breaching targeted financial sanctions measures`
    `not copying a suspicious transaction disclosure to the Registrar`
    `disobeying a written direction`
    `giving false information`
    `obstructing an investigation`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unregistered dealing` THEN 75000
    WHEN `failing to file a cash transaction report` THEN 20000
    WHEN `not copying a suspicious transaction disclosure to the Registrar` THEN 20000
    WHEN `disobeying a written direction` THEN 20000
    WHEN `giving false information` THEN 50000
    WHEN `obstructing an investigation` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 100000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unregistered dealing` THEN 3
    WHEN `failing to file a cash transaction report` THEN 2
    WHEN `giving false information` THEN 2
    WHEN `obstructing an investigation` THEN 2
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum composition sum` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2
